  "job": "Shatters her own blade into the enemy line, fights fast with the hilt, then swings it whole again.",
  "difficulty": 2,
  "lore": "Ervet cast her greatsword in dawnglass to be unbreakable, and spent a year finding out she had made it wrong. A blade that cannot break cannot be mended, and a blade that cannot be mended cannot be handed on. Now she breaks it herself, on purpose, in front of whoever stands closest, and fights with what is left in her fist. The shards sing when they land. She says that is the sound of an idea ending, and the whole blade is the sound of it starting again. Aubade duelists argue about whether that is craft or showing off. Ervet does not argue; she has a sword to put back together.",
